  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1130 AM MDT Tue May 26 2026\n\nDrier air has settled into our area, bringing with it clear skies\nand near-to-slightly below average temperatures for the area on \nTuesday, though there will be sufficient moisture for a chance of \nspotty showers in eastern Otero and northeastern Hudspeth \nCounties. Winds will be light and variable. Southwest flow aloft \nwill keep us dry throughout the week, though lurking moisture to \nour east will give the Sacramento Mountains and eastern Hudspeth \nCounty a chance of precipitation.\n\nTemperatures for the rest of the week will stay between the mid \n80s to the low 90s as we transition from May to June, still near-\nto- slightly below average temperatures for this time of year. \nRelative humidities for most of southern New Mexico and El Paso \nCounty will hover around 10-20% for the rest of the week. The \nmoisture to our east is worth keeping an eye on, as though the \nsouthwesterly flow aloft will keep it east of the Franklins, there\nwill be a slight chance for an intrusion of moisture in the lower\nRio Grande Valley next Monday.",
